# Basic consequences of upper Minkowski dimension

The dimension is defined as an infimum of admissible covering exponents.  For
sets of radii in `[1,2]`, this file records both the elementary ambient
admissible exponent and the standard ``arbitrarily small loss'' consequence
of the infimum definition.
